#
# RK3588 AMP board options (sourced via $(DEVICE_PATH)/Kconfig).
#

config RK3588_OPENAMP
    bool "Enable OpenAMP/rpmsg (MICA) support"
    default n
    depends on PLATFORM_RK3588_M
    select COMPONENT_OPENAMP
    help
      Bring up open-amp + libmetal on the RTOS side and register the
      rpmsg-tty endpoint for the Linux MICA framework (/dev/ttyRPMSG0).
      Interrupt notification uses SGI 7 (MICA convention).

config MCS
    bool "Enable MCS hybrid deployment (AMP slave alongside Linux master)"
    default n
    depends on PLATFORM_RK3588_M
    select RK3588_OPENAMP
    help
      MCS hybrid deployment: this core (CPU7, Cortex-A76) runs as the AMP
      slave started and stopped by the Linux master mcs_km driver, sharing
      the debug UART (Linux ttyFIQ0 console) with the master. When enabled:
        - UartInit keeps the shared UART untouched (polled TX only);
        - the shell does not poll UART RX (input comes over rpmsg tty);
        - the mica/rpmsg service task is created at boot.
      When disabled the board owns the UART itself (standalone bring-up).

config RK3588_UART
    bool "Enable the RK3588 UART driver (Modbus-RTU oriented, uart_drv.h API)"
    default n
    depends on PLATFORM_RK3588_M
    depends on PLATFORM_HWI_WITH_ARG
    help
      Interrupt-driven DW 8250 UART driver for UART1~UART9 (board/uart.c,
      API in include/uart_drv.h): per-port RX/TX ring buffers + semaphore
      blocking semantics, line-synchronous write (LSR TEMT anchored),
      CRU/IOC/GIC profile bring-up, and the uart_test shell command.
      Independent of the console driver (uart_porting.c): the protocol
      layer passes a port id (1..9) and gets it initialized - UART2 is
      shared with the Linux master console, caller-owned risk.
      RS485 direction control is out of scope (auto-direction
      transceiver); the optional RX echo suppression is a profile flag.

# Real-time data-plane options (MCS_NET / MCS_CAN) live with the board
# sources one level down; rsource is relative to this file (this file is
# reached as $(DEVICE_PATH)/Kconfig through the board symlink).
rsource "board/Kconfig"
